        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Seán Smyth, Mary Colum\n- Places: Straide, County Mayo, Galway, Connacht, Ireland\n- Organizations: Róisín Dubh\n- Topics: Irish music, literature\n\nFacts:\n- Mary Colum was born as Mary Maguire on June 14, 1884, and she was an Irish literary critic and author who also co-founded a literary journal.\n- Seán Smyth was born in Straide, County Mayo, and he later lived in Galway.\n- Seán Smyth became an All-Ireland champion on both fiddle and whistle.\n- Galway is a city in the West of Ireland in the province of Connacht.\n- The Róisín Dubh is an established live music venue in Galway, Ireland.\n- Mary Colum died on October 22, 1957.",
